// K7 regression, found by the Scapy fuzzer: payload past the peer's FIN is discarded
// silently; its ACK still acknowledges transmitted data. RFC 9293 3.10.7.4, seventh
// step, says to ignore segment text after FIN.
// - Ten bytes echo, then the peer's FIN at 11 moves Zhida to CloseWait. tap-echo
//   closes, moving Zhida to LastAck and sending its FIN at 11.
// - The overlapping payload at 6:26 acknowledges the echo (ack 11), but not Zhida's
//   FIN. Its payload is discarded: no new stream data, ACK of that data, or RST.
// - The next ACK (seq 12, ack 12) closes LastAck; a new SYN gets a SYN-ACK.
// packetdrill fills payloads with zero bytes; the check is on sequence numbers only.

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    < P. 1:11(10) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1:11(10) ack 11 win 32768
+0.1  < F. 11:11(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    > . 11:11(0) ack 12 win 32768
+0    > F. 11:11(0) ack 12 win 32768
+0.1  < P. 6:26(20) ack 11 win 502
+0.1  < . 12:12(0) ack 12 win 502

+0.1  < S 5000:5000(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 5001 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
